[agent:result] """Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform (GCP) checker adapter — grader-side reads through the project.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform's feature store is BigQuery-backed: a Feature Group is defined over a
[agent:result] BigQuery table, so feature/training-dataset reads go straight through the
[agent:result] BigQuery client (`SELECT * FROM <project>.<dataset>.<name>`) — the same path a
[agent:result] the platform consumer uses. Model/job/endpoint/vector-search reads go through the
[agent:result] aiplatform SDK. Native Vector Search (Matching Engine) means get_vector_store
[agent:result] reports native_ann=True (unlike SageMaker/Azure).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Auth: a service-account key at GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS (standard ADC);
[agent:result] GCP_PROJECT / GCP_LOCATION / GCP_BQ_DATASET scope the reads. SDKs imported
[agent:result] lazily so this module imports without google-cloud-* installed.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] NOTE: live-validate against a real project before trusting A3–A5 — the BigQuery
[agent:result] table-naming and feature-group→BQ mapping are convention-based here.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] CLI (for live probing):
[agent:result]     python -m evals.adapters.gcp describe-fg --name transactions
[agent:result]     python -m evals.adapters.gcp read-fg --name transactions --out /tmp/fg.csv
[agent:result] """
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] from __future__ import annotations
[agent:result] 
