[agent] **What was done, entirely on-platform (BigQuery):**
[agent] 1. Loaded all six source CSVs into the run dataset via `bq load` (`raw_transactions`, `raw_transactions_late`, `raw_profiles`, `raw_activity`, `raw_account_health`, `raw_labels`).
[agent] 2. Ran a single BigQuery SQL job to build the training dataset:
[agent]    - **Transactions** = `raw_transactions` `UNION ALL` `raw_transactions_late` (the late-arriving export is included as part of the same data).
[agent]    - **Point-in-time correctness**: for each `(account_id, label_time)`, each feature is joined on `account_id` with `event_time <= label_time`, then the most-recent qualifying row is selected via `ROW_NUMBER() … ORDER BY event_time DESC` + `QUALIFY = 1`. Rows with `event_time` after `label_time` can never be selected — no future leakage, in any table. `amount`/`balance` come from the same latest transaction row.
[agent]    - `LEFT JOIN`s from labels guarantee one row per label row.
